repository-code: 'https://github.com/ericks-rs/yolo-aksara-jawa-dhcd'
abstract: >-
  Code, per-run configuration files, per-epoch training logs, and per-seed
  results for a study asking whether the C2PSA attention block in modern
  YOLO releases earns its place on isolated character classification. The
  repository also contains the leakage-corrected split for the public
  Aksara Jawa dataset, in which 25.00 percent of the distributed
  validation images are augmented variants of training images.
keywords:
  - YOLO
  - attention mechanism
  - character classification
  - Javanese script
  - Devanagari
  - ablation study
  - data leakage
license: MIT
